==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 3~14 seconds<sup>90f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 3~14 seconds<sup>90f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 6~14 seconds<sup>180f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 6~14 seconds<sup>180f~420f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 60~80 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 66.67~100 seconds<sup>2,000f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Le'boin]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 140 seconds<sup>4,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Le'boin]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Le'boin]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The main threats of this stage appear quite late, so rushing is highly recommended. [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cat]] should make quick work of this stage once the Le'boin comes out; since he spawns without a boss shockwave, you just need to keep the enemies pushed back without killing them and the Zang Roo will never spawn, making the stage MUCH easier.

If you do have to fight Zang Roo, be very careful. With a lengthy burrow range and rapid Area Attacks, she will shred your backline and head straight for the [[Cat Base]], which may be unprotected after dealing with the Le'boin.

With Zir Zeal and Zory messing up your backline, you will be fighting [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] on at least two fronts, if not three, and will need to save certain [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] for when they do eventually burrow.

